WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.480 --> 00:00:19.505
The Caterpillar had said that one side of the mushroom would make Alice grow.

2
00:00:20.505 --> 00:00:22.345
The other side would make her shrink.

3
00:00:23.386 --> 00:00:26.847
Then he'd disappeared before Alice could ask any questions.

4
00:00:30.428 --> 00:00:31.808
Alice studied the mushroom.

5
00:00:37.196 --> 00:00:39.178
"How am I supposed to know which side does which?

6
00:00:40.038 --> 00:00:44.062
The mushroom cap is round, so it doesn't have a left side or a right side."

7
00:00:45.823 --> 00:00:47.845
There was only one way to find out.

8
00:00:49.166 --> 00:00:54.030
Alice stretched her arms around the mushroom and broke off a piece with each hand.

9
00:00:54.050 --> 00:00:57.813
"But which piece makes me grow?"

10
00:00:58.834 --> 00:01:00.995
Alice looked from one hand to the other.

11
00:01:01.836 --> 00:01:05.279
She finally decided to try the piece in her right hand.

12
00:01:08.544 --> 00:01:14.509
The next moment her chin hit something hard.

13
00:01:15.430 --> 00:01:16.391
It was her foot!

14
00:01:17.532 --> 00:01:22.075
Alice was frightened, but she managed to try the mushroom piece in her left hand.

15
00:01:22.095 --> 00:01:26.019
"That's better!"

16
00:01:26.479 --> 00:01:29.081
Alice said as her head started to rise.

17
00:01:32.544 --> 00:01:36.868
But her delight changed to panic when she couldn't see her shoulders.

18
00:01:38.348 --> 00:01:43.892
When she looked down, all she saw were her long neck and some green leaves.

19
00:01:45.213 --> 00:01:48.696
She didn't realize those were the tops of trees.

20
00:01:48.716 --> 00:01:51.458
"Where have my hands gone?"

21
00:01:51.818 --> 00:01:52.559
Alice asked.

22
00:01:53.640 --> 00:01:57.162
She couldn't see them below the leaves, so she bent her neck.

23
00:01:59.484 --> 00:02:01.446
"My neck is so flexible!

24
00:02:02.466 --> 00:02:04.168
It's almost like being a serpent.

25
00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:09.663
Oh!" Alice exclaimed in surprise as a bird flew at her face.

26
00:02:15.087 --> 00:02:16.207
the Pigeon screamed.

27
00:02:16.227 --> 00:02:18.489
"I'm not a serpent!"

28
00:02:18.769 --> 00:02:20.010
Alice said angrily.

29
00:02:20.030 --> 00:02:21.591
"Leave me alone!"

30
00:02:21.611 --> 00:02:27.274
"No matter where I make my nest, serpents bother me!"

31
00:02:28.195 --> 00:02:29.936
The Pigeon sounded angry.

32
00:02:31.280 --> 00:02:35.022
"Night and day I must be on the lookout for serpents.

33
00:02:35.883 --> 00:02:37.824
I haven't slept in three weeks!"

34
00:02:39.185 --> 00:02:42.967
"I'm very sorry that you've been annoyed by serpents," Alice began.

35
00:02:42.987 --> 00:02:51.111
"But—" "I made my nest in the tallest tree, thinking I'd be free of the serpents," the Pigeon

36
00:02:51.191 --> 00:02:55.874
said. "But then you came wiggling down from the sky!

37
00:02:56.695 --> 00:02:58.295
Go away, Serpent!"

38
00:02:59.696 --> 00:03:02.317
"I'm not a serpent," Alice said.

39
00:03:02.337 --> 00:03:07.440
"I'm a I mean, I'm a "Well!

40
00:03:08.180 --> 00:03:09.620
What are you?"

41
00:03:10.201 --> 00:03:11.341
the Pigeon demanded.

42
00:03:11.361 --> 00:03:14.943
"What are you trying to say?"

43
00:03:14.963 --> 00:03:19.785
"I I'm a little girl," Alice finally said.

44
00:03:21.526 --> 00:03:26.468
She'd undergone so many changes, she wasn't sure what she was anymore.

45
00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:34.204
"I've seen lots of little girls but never one with such a long neck."

46
00:03:34.844 --> 00:03:37.025
The Pigeon looked at her skeptically.

47
00:03:37.045 --> 00:03:42.268
"No, you're a serpent, and you can't deny it.

48
00:03:43.189 --> 00:03:47.271
Next you'll be telling me that you've never eaten an egg."

49
00:03:47.291 --> 00:03:55.676
"I have eaten an egg," Alice admitted for she was a truthful child.

50
00:03:56.728 --> 00:03:58.990
"Little girls eat eggs as often as serpents do."

51
00:03:59.010 --> 00:04:03.514
"I don't believe that," the Pigeon said firmly.

52
00:04:03.534 --> 00:04:09.399
"And whether you're a girl or a serpent, you're looking for eggs."

53
00:04:09.419 --> 00:04:13.042
"I'm not looking for eggs.

54
00:04:13.942 --> 00:04:16.845
But if I were looking for them, I wouldn't want yours."

55
00:04:19.087 --> 00:04:21.809
Alice stamped her foot, and the ground shook.

56
00:04:21.829 --> 00:04:24.952
"I don't like raw eggs!"

57
00:04:26.428 --> 00:04:28.109
"Then go away!"

58
00:04:28.889 --> 00:04:33.112
The Pigeon still sounded angry as she settled into her nest again.

59
00:04:37.374 --> 00:04:42.556
Alice tried to crouch among the trees, but her neck kept getting tangled in branches.

60
00:04:42.576 --> 00:04:48.519
"I need to get back to my original size," she said to herself.

61
00:04:57.636 --> 00:05:03.518
Slowly and carefully, Alice nibbled from one piece of mushroom and then the other.

62
00:05:08.759 --> 00:05:11.620
At last, she was the correct size.

63
00:05:11.640 --> 00:05:14.161
"That's much better!"

64
00:05:14.721 --> 00:05:16.862
Alice said as she began to walk through the woods.

65
00:05:20.583 --> 00:05:25.344
Suddenly she came upon a space surrounding a house about four feet high.

66
00:05:26.756 --> 00:05:29.299
"I don't know who lives there," Alice said.

67
00:05:29.319 --> 00:05:34.544
"But they're sure to be smaller than I am, and I'll frighten them at this size."

68
00:05:36.086 --> 00:05:41.351
So Alice ate some more from the mushroom until she was only nine inches high.
